{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":491},{"id":2,"agency":3,"agency_full":4,"sector":5,"dest":6,"color":7,"year":8,"status":9,"departure_date":10,"arrival_date":11,"transit_days":12,"vehicle":13,"payload":14,"delta_v":15,"data_quality":16,"credit":17,"links":18,"flight_data_quality":33,"fleet_refs":34,"flight":40,"name":463,"type":464,"first":465,"description":466,"events":467,"vehicle_stage":42},"slim","JAXA","Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency","gov","MOON","#003087",2024,"FLOWN","2023-09-06","2024-01-19",135,"H-IIA 202","730 kg launch mass; 200 kg lander; 2 micro-rovers (LEV-1, LEV-2)","~3 km/s","good","© JAXA — Smart Lander for Investigating Moon. Demonstrated pinpoint landing within 100 m of target (vs km-scale standard). Long transit used a low-energy ballistic trajectory to save propellant.",[19,23,26,30],{"l":20,"u":21,"t":22},"SLIM — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smart_Lander_for_Investigating_Moon","intro",{"l":24,"u":25,"t":22},"SLIM (JAXA)","https://global.jaxa.jp/projects/sas/slim/",{"l":27,"u":28,"t":29},"小型月着陸実証機 SLIM (ISAS/JAXA)","https://www.isas.jaxa.jp/en/missions/spacecraft/past/slim.html","core",{"l":31,"u":32,"t":29},"SLIM — 日本語版ウィキペディア","https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/SLIM","measured",[35,38],{"id":36,"role":37},"h-iia","launcher",{"id":2,"role":39},"spacecraft",{"launch":41,"cruise":45,"arrival":48,"totals":58,"events":60,"cislunar_profile":96},{"vehicle_stage":42,"mass_at_tli_kg":43,"source":44,"departure":39},"H-IIA 2nd stage",730,"JAXA SLIM Project Brief (2023)",{"tcm_count":46,"source":47},4,"JAXA SLIM Mission Operations Report; long ballistic transit for propellant economy",{"v_infinity_km_s":49,"periapsis_km":50,"inclination_deg":51,"orbit_insertion_dv_km_s":52,"source":53,"entry_velocity_km_s":54,"edl_system":55,"edl_duration_s":56,"touchdown_velocity_ms":57},0.82,100,90,0.75,"JAXA SLIM LOI Report (2023-12)",1.69,"powered",1016,1,{"total_dv_km_s":59,"source":44},3,[61,66,71,76,80,83,87,92],{"met_days":62,"type":63,"label":64,"description":65},0,"launch","Launch — H-IIA","Tanegashima, Japan, 2023-09-06. SLIM (Smart Lander for Investigating Moon) — JAXA's first lunar landing attempt. Designed to demonstrate \"pinpoint\" landing — better than 100-m accuracy versus the kilometres of dispersion in earlier Moon landings.",{"met_days":67,"type":68,"label":69,"description":70},0.05,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-lunar injection","H-IIA upper stage burn places SLIM on a long-duration energy-efficient transfer.",{"met_days":72,"type":73,"label":74,"description":75},25.34,"tcm","TCM-1","First post-TMI cleanup.",{"met_days":77,"type":73,"label":78,"description":79},30,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":81,"type":73,"label":82,"description":79},45.13,"TCM-3",{"met_days":84,"type":73,"label":85,"description":86},64.92,"TCM-4 — final pre-LOI","Final approach targeting before lunar orbit insertion.",{"met_days":88,"type":89,"label":90,"description":91},110,"arrival","Lunar orbit insertion","2023-12-25. Captured into a 600 × 4,000 km polar orbit. JAXA spent ~30 days lowering perilune to ~15 km for the descent.",{"met_days":12,"type":93,"label":94,"description":95},"edl_or_oi","Lunar pinpoint landing — Shioli crater","2024-01-19. SLIM landed about 10 m from its target point inside Shioli crater (13.3°S, 25.2°E) — the most precise lunar landing of any mission ever. Japan becomes the 5th nation to soft-land on the Moon. The landing posture was off-nominal (a thrust-vector anomaly tipped the lander on its side), but the solar panels later caught sunlight 9 days into the lunar day and the mission returned surface science.",{"source_tier":97,"parking_orbit":98,"tli":101,"translunar":103,"lunar_arrival":105,"return":108,"waypoints_km":110,"waypoints_source":460,"lunar_orbits":461},"tier_1_5_hybrid",{"altitude_km":99,"inclination_deg":100,"revs":57},250,31,{"dv_kms":102},3.1,{"type":104},"spiral",{"type":106,"altitude_km":107,"inclination_deg":51,"periselene_km":107},"orbit_a